    {
      "id": "p0034-b003",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "As an example, an important island in the One Piece series named ラフテル (rafuteru) was introduced in 1999. Because the Japanese language doesn’t distinguish between “L” and “R” sounds, and because the series’ creator wasn’t involved in the translation process, English translators originally called the island “Raftel”, hoping this literal transcription was correct. In 2019, with the series still chugging along, it was finally revealed that the creator intended the name to be “Laugh Tale” all along.",
        "raw": "As an example, an important island in the One Piece series named 777-Jv\n(rafuteru) was introduced in 1999. Because the Japanese language doesn't\ndistinguish between \"L\" and \"R\" sounds, and because the series' creator wasn't\ninvolved in the translation process, English translators originally called the\nisland \"Raftel\", hoping this literal transcription was correct. In 2019, with the\nseries still chugging along, it was finally revealed that the creator intended the\nname to be \"Laugh Tale\" all along.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en",
          "ja"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29131623,
          0.21015714,
          0.89369382,
          0.33247857
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.28929936,
          0.20944286,
          0.90150918,
          0.33355
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          8,
          11,
          13,
          15,
          17,
          19,
          21
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "例如，《One Piece》在1999年提到一座重要的岛，名叫ラフテル（rafuteru）。日语不区分 L 和 R 的发音，而原作者没有参与翻译，英语译者便先将岛名拼成 Raftel，希望这种直接音译是对的。到2019年，故事仍在连载，大家才终于得知：作者从一开始想的就是 Laugh Tale（笑谈）。",
        "status": "draft",
